governor asks: I can make the output easier to read in several ways. Which of these do you want (pick any)?
1. Status markers: show each todo as "[ ] 3. Buy milk" or "[x] 3. Buy milk" instead of the current style.
2. Aligned columns: pad IDs and titles so that the due dates line up, e.g. " 3  Buy milk        due 2024-05-01".
3. Grouping/sorting: show open todos first and done todos last, or sort by due date.
4. Summary line: add a footer such as "2 open, 1 done".
5. Empty-list message: print "No todos." instead of blank output.
6. Colour (ANSI): for example, dim the done items and show overdue dates in red. This only makes sense if the output is a terminal.
Also, should the "add" and "complete" confirmation messages change too, or only the list output? If you have an exact example of the output you want, please paste it.

